          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em excisive (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            which sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
            squares to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            squares. If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+types"} finite homotopy types
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excision"} excision
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized homotopy
          %p
            Moreover, if here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            is instead
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"}> spectrum objects
            ) – essentially by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            – and those without such restriction are equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{H}
            %a{:href => "n-excisive+functor#nExcisiveFunctorsFormInfinityTopos"} here
            at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+functor"} n-excisive functor
            and at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+locus"} Joyal locus
          %p
            As such, excisive functors are the lowest nontrivial stage in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie-Taylor+tower"} Goodwillie-Taylor tower
            that approximates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} classifying (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}[X_\bullet]
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} n-excisive (∞,1)-functors
          %h2#definition Definition
          #ExcisiveFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              out of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} finite (∞,1)-colimits
              is
              %strong excisive
              if it takes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pushout"} (∞,1)-pushout
              squares in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              squares
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            %p
              This is the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
              case of the concept of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} n-excisive (∞,1)-functor
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} HigherAlg, def. 1.4.2.1.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#SpectrumObjects Spectrum objects
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+types"} finite homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} finite (∞,1)-colimits
            from the point. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            finite homotopy types.
          #SpectraAsExcisiveFunctors.num_defn
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              are equivalently
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} reduced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} excisive (∞,1)-functor
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (Sometimes, e.g. in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} Lurie, def. 1.4.2.8
          %p
            A proof of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpectraAsExcisiveFunctors"}
            passing through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            for excisive
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+model+structure"} Bousfield-Friedlander model structure
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Lydakis98"}> Lydakis 98
            ), see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "model+structure+for+excisive+functors#ModelStructureForSpectra"} Relation to BF-model structure on sequential spectra
          %p
            The idea of the equivalence is as follows. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be a reduced excisive functor. For each
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \in \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            and write
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{n} \coloneqq E(S^n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; S^{n+1}
                  }
          %p
            and since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            sends them to homotopy pullbacks with the point going to the point, this gives equivalences
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Ω
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_n \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \Omega E_{n+1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
            have the structure of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega+spectrum"} Omega spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            and the value of the excisive functor on any finite homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty(E \wedge X)
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} Lurie, remark 1.4.3.3
          #RelationToGeneralizedHomologyTheories.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The traditional definition of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
              is as a functor on (finite) homotopy types with values in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
              says that these all arise from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              via taking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+products"} smash products
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto E_\bullet(X) \coloneqq \pi_\bullet(E \wedge X)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phantom+maps"} phantom maps
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence
              between spectra and generalized homology theories.
            %p
              In view of this, the proof of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpectraAsExcisiveFunctors"}
              may be thought of saying that this mismatch is fixed by refining homotopy groups by full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↦
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \Omega^\infty(E\wedge X)
            %p
              Notice also that spectra realized as excisive functors this way are in the spirit of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate-free+spectra"} coordinate-free spectra
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            For the moment we focus on properties of the case of excisive functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} = \mathbf{H}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Exc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mi fin
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Exc(\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}, \mathbf{H}) \simeq T \mathbf{H} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
                  \\,.
          #ClassifyingToposForPointedObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+types"} finite homotopy types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              a given
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn ∞
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Grpd
                              %mi fin
                              %mrow
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi PSh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Grpd
                              %mi fin
                              %mrow
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    [\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}, \mathbf{H}]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    PSh((\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/})^{op}, \mathbf{H})
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} classifying (∞,1)-topos
              (over
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
          %h3#ReflectionAndExcisiveApproximation Reflection and excisive approximation
          #P1.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T_1 \colon \mathbf{H}[X_\ast] \longrightarrow \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
            %p for the functor given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \mapsto \Omega_{E(\ast)} E(\Sigma(-))
                    \\,.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi n
                    %msubsup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_1 \coloneqq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{n} T_1^{n}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              of the iterations of this functor, with respect to the canonical comparison map.
          %p
            Unwinding the definition and using that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            is equivalently the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "join%20of%20topological%20spaces#JoinWith0Sphere"} join with the 0-sphere
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Goodwillie03"} Goodwillie 91, p. 657 (13 of 67)
          #PnLocalizes.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The inclusion of excisive functors into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}[X_*]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
              with reflector given by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1
              from def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#P1"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 1
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \mathbf{H}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{P_1}{\longleftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
          %p
            This is due (in the generality of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/n-excisive+functor#nExcisiveApproximation"} n-excisive functor – n-Excisive Approximation and reflection
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Goodwillie91"} Goodwillie 91, theorem 1.8
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"} Lurie, theorem 6.1.1.10, construction 6.1.1.27
          #ExcisiveApproximation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              have finite colimits and a terminal object and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              be differentiable.
            %p
              The excisive approximation of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+functor"} reduced functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-colimit"} (infinity,1)-colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P_1 F
                    \\simeq
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow_{\mathrlap{k}}}{\lim}
                    ( \Omega^k \circ F \circ \Sigma^k)
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              denote
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping"} looping
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              and in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HigherAlg"}> Lurie, example 6.1.1.28
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Under the equivalence to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
              in prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpectraAsExcisiveFunctors"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExcisiveApproximation"}
              is the standard formula for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrification"} spectrification
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prespectra"} prespectra
          %h3#CharacterizationViaAGenericStableObject Characterization via a generic stable object
          %p
            We discuss a characterization of excisive functors on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            a generic pointed object to become a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AnelBiedermanFinsterJoyal17b"} Anel-Biederman-Finster-Joyal
          %p
            For a slick formulation, we use a generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
            to pointed powers:
          #PointedPower.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an object in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_\ast \in \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
              a pointed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} finite ∞-groupoid
              %em pointed power
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{S_\ast} \in \mathcal{C}
            %p
              is the object which is the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              under the essentially unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/})^\op \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            %p
              which preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              and sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ←
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 \leftarrow \ast
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\ast \to \ast
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Excisive functors
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mi fin
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/} \longrightarrow \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExcisiveFunctor"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassifyingToposForPointedObjects"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mo *
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∈
                        %mn ∞
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mi fin
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\Sigma \Omega (X_\ast^{S_\ast}) \longrightarrow X_\ast^{S_\ast}
                    \\right\}_{S \in \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}}
                    \\,,
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\ast}^{S_\ast}
              is the pointed power, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedPower"}
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\ast \in \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi Ω
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \mathbf{H}\simeq \mathbf{H}[X_\ast][ (\Sigma \Omega X_\ast^\bullet \to X_\ast^\bullet)^{-1} ]
                    \\,.
            %p
              In other words, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
              are those objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
              which regard each finite pointed power of the generic pointed object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\ast
              as a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn ∞
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mi fin
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ↪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(K) \in (\infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/})^{op} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R(K)^S \simeq R(S \cdot K)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that the generic pointed object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
              is that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
              by the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\ast = R(S^0)
                    \\,.
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                      %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\ast^S \simeq R(S)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+lemma"} (∞,1)-Yoneda lemma
              we have for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathbf{H}[X_\ast]
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo *
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Hom( \Sigma \Omega R(K), E )
                    \&amp;\simeq
                    \\Omega_{E(\ast)} Hom(\Omega R(K),E)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\Omega_{E(\ast)} Hom( R(\Sigma K), E )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\Omega_{E(\ast)} E(\Sigma K)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in \infty Grpd_{fin}^{\ast/}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mn 1
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Hom(\Sigma \Omega R(K) \to R(K), E)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    ( E(K) \longrightarrow  \Omega(\Sigma K) )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (E \to T_1 E)(K)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where in the last line we observe that the expression is that for the comparison map in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#P1"}
            %p
              This means that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              are precisely those
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              for which the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \longrightarrow T_1 E
            %p
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#P1"}
              is an equivalence. With this the statement follows from theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PnLocalizes"}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} exact (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} n-excisive (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-excisive+functors"} n-excisive functors
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Goodwillie91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"}> Thomas Goodwillie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Calculus II, Analytic functors
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+tower"} Taylor tower
            formed by
            = succeed "-excisive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#Goodwillie03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Goodwillie"}> Thomas Goodwillie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Calculus III: Taylor Series
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0310481"} arXiv:math/0310481
          %p
            A discussion in the general abstract context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#HigherAlg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 6.1.1 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p Review includes:
          %ul
            %li#Harpaz2013
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
              , section 5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Introduction to stable
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HarpazStableInfinityCategory2013.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On excisive 1-functors for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+G-spectra"} genuine G-spectra
            (i.e. in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} proper
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#DHLPS19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Degrijse"}> Dieter Degrijse
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Hausmann"} Markus Hausmann
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+L%C3%BCck"} Wolfgang Lück
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Irakli+Patchkoria"} Irakli Patchkoria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
              = succeed "," do
                %em Proper equivariant stable homotopy theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.00779"} arXiv:1908.00779
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
            was given in
          %ul
            %li#Lydakis98
              Lydakis,
              %em Simplicial functors and stable homotopy theory
              Preprint, available via Hopf archive, 1998 (
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Lydakis/s_functors.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#AnelBiedermanFinsterJoyal17b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathieu+Anel"}> Mathieu Anel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Biedermann"} Georg Biedermann
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Finster"} Eric Finster
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
              %em Goodwillie’s Calculus of Functors and Higher Topos Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.09632"}> arXiv:1703.09632
              )
